From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:31:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Bring RingCentral Analytics' performance report into the
 Service Quality tab

The tab only asked Analytics about call queues, so an account whose calls go
straight to people's extensions saw nothing but a note telling them to unlock
live data they already had.

- Worker: /api/performance asks the Business Analytics timeline for every
  user, one point per day, in the dashboard's time zone (falling back to UTC
  if RingCentral rejects the zone), and maps direction, first response,
  result, company hours, hold/transfer actions and ringing/talk/hold time.
- Dashboard: the report imports with the other datasets (and for the prior
  period), and the Service Quality tab shows inbound answered, not answered,
  outbound connected, talk and ring time, after-hours share, a daily
  answered trend, time by part of call, and a sortable per-user table. The
  queue view stays underneath for accounts that have queue data.
- The empty-state text no longer tells a connected viewer to unlock live data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
